---
/* =========================================================
   PROFILE LINKS

   The icon row that used to sit at the foot of the home page,
   moved here as labelled buttons.

   Labels rather than bare icons: on a contact page the point
   is to be unambiguous, and the ORCID and ResearchGate marks
   are not recognisable to everyone the way GitHub's is. The
   label also means the link works if an icon fails to load.

   Email and the CV PDF are deliberately absent. Email is the
   primary action at the top of the page, and repeating it as
   one tile of seven flattened the hierarchy the card above
   builds; the CV is a download from this site rather than a
   profile elsewhere, and both are linked from the section's
   own paragraph instead.

   One flat row, not groups. With those two removed the five
   that remain are all the same kind of thing - an external
   profile with a handle behind it - so subheadings were more
   chrome than five items can carry. Order does the work
   instead: the two that a collaborator checks first lead.

   No secondary text on the tiles either. Only two of the five
   had an identifier worth showing, which made those cards
   taller than the rest; the ORCID iD moved to the details
   list on the page, where the other identifying facts live.
========================================================= */

import profile from "../data/cvheader.json";

const links = [
  {
    label: "Google Scholar",
    href: "https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=FHoe1FQAAAAJ",
    icon: "googlescholar.svg"
  },
  {
    label: "ORCID",
    href: `https://orcid.org/${profile.orcid}`,
    icon: "orcid.svg"
  },
  {
    label: "GitHub",
    href: "https://github.com/eirikmn",
    icon: "github.svg"
  },
  {
    label: "ResearchGate",
    href: "https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Eirik-Myrvoll-Nilsen",
    icon: "researchgate.svg"
  },
  {
    label: "LinkedIn",
    href: "https://www.linkedin.com/in/eirik-myrvoll-nilsen-816b7379/",
    icon: "linkedin.svg"
  }
];
---

<ul class="profile-links">
  {links.map((link) => (
    <li>
      <a
        class="profile-link"
        href={link.href}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer me"
      >
        <span
          class="profile-icon"
          style={`--icon: url('/icons/${link.icon}')`}
          aria-hidden="true"
        ></span>
        <span>{link.label}</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  ))}
</ul>

<style>
/* Flex rather than an equal-width grid.

   The grid forced every tile to one width, which meant five items never
   filled their rows evenly - 4 + 1 at full width, 3 + 2 below that - and
   the orphan sat alone against empty tracks. It also padded "ORCID" out
   to the width of "Google Scholar", so half the tiles were mostly empty
   space.

   Sizing each tile to its own label lets the five flow and wrap without
   a ragged last row, and the widths vary the way the labels do. */
.profile-links {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 1.25rem 0 0;

  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.6rem;
}

.profile-link {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;

  padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;

  border: 1px solid var(--border-ui);
  border-radius: 8px;

  color: var(--text);
  text-decoration: none;
  font-size: 0.9rem;

  transition: border-color 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease,
              background 0.2s ease;
}

.profile-link:hover {
  border-color: var(--accent);
  color: var(--accent);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent);
}

/* =========================
   ICONS

   Masked rather than filtered.

   The previous version tinted with
     invert(48%) sepia(90%) saturate(1000%) hue-rotate(180deg)
   which never referenced --accent at all: it produced an approximate
   blue that only resembled it by coincidence. Worse, light and dark use
   different accents while the filter chain was the same in both, so it
   could not match either reliably.

   A mask paints the shape with `background: currentColor`, so the icon
   takes whatever colour the link already has - the theme's text colour
   at rest, the exact --accent on hover, with no second set of rules for
   dark mode and nothing to keep in sync if the accent changes.
========================= */

.profile-icon {
  width: 22px;
  height: 22px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  display: block;

  background: currentColor;

  -webkit-mask-image: var(--icon);
  mask-image: var(--icon);
  -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
  mask-repeat: no-repeat;
  -webkit-mask-position: center;
  mask-position: center;
  -webkit-mask-size: contain;
  mask-size: contain;

  transition: transform 0.2s ease;
}

.profile-link:hover .profile-icon {
  transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.05);
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .profile-icon {
    transition: none;
  }

  .profile-link:hover .profile-icon {
    transform: none;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .profile-links {
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .profile-link {
    padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .profile-icon {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
  }
}
</style>
